---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SocialLinks from '../components/SocialLinks.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import headshot from '../assets/images/LI_headshot.jpeg';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: siteConfig.author.name,
  url: siteConfig.url,
  jobTitle: 'Product Leader & Builder',
  sameAs: [siteConfig.social.github, siteConfig.social.linkedin, siteConfig.social.twitter],
};
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Ben Shoemaker on product leadership, data, and building with AI. From employer products at Indeed to AI products and independent projects." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[240px_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-8 lg:gap-16">
      <aside>
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-12">
          <Image src={headshot} alt="Ben Shoemaker" width={240} height={240} class="w-24 h-24 sm:w-40 sm:h-40 lg:w-60 lg:h-60 rounded-xl object-cover mb-5" />
          <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Ben Shoemaker</p>
          <SocialLinks />
          <a href="/services" class="inline-flex py-3 mt-3 text-sm text-accent hover:underline">Working together &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <article class="min-w-0 max-w-[68ch]">
        <header class="mb-10">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-5">About</h1>
          <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl leading-relaxed text-text-primary">I'm Ben. I work on products, data, and AI.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">I've spent much of my career figuring out what people need, building teams and products around it, and working out whether we're actually helping. These days, a lot of that involves building with AI.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="space-y-10 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <section aria-labelledby="background">
            <h2 id="background" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">From data to product</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p>I spent about twelve years at Indeed. I started as a data analyst, then moved into product, building tools that helped employers manage candidates and hire people. That meant understanding how a small-business owner actually works, and making the software fit.</p>
              <p>Later, I helped build and lead the Employer Data &amp; Analytics organization, partnering with engineering and managing product managers. We built customer-feedback systems, shared metrics, and data products that teams across Indeed used to make decisions. ASK'EM, our survey platform, and Connections, a company-level engagement metric, were two big pieces of that work.</p>
              <p>That experience still shapes how I think. A metric is useful when it helps someone decide what to do. A platform is useful when other people can build on it without having to come through you.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="ai-work">
            <h2 id="ai-work" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">Building with AI</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p>More recently, I've worked on AI products in smaller teams. Through Zencohen, I worked on a consumer conversational-AI product, helping plan its launch and using early user behavior to understand where the experience was breaking down.</p>
              <p>At Devplan, I led product work across customer discovery, self-serve onboarding, and AI quality. I worked with engineering to get the onboarding experience into production, then used AI tools to implement specific signup and setup improvements with engineering review. I also worked on how the AI generated and edited documents, testing changes against actual outputs and checking what users would see.</p>
              <p>Alongside that, I've co-built a PropTech startup and made my own tools, including <a href="/projects#vibescaffold" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">VibeScaffold</a> and an <a href="/projects#ai-coding-project-base" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">open-source AI coding toolkit</a>. Building things myself gives me a way to test the ideas I write about.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="working-style">
            <h2 id="working-style" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">How I like to work</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p>I think teams do their best work when they understand the outcome they're trying to reach and have room to figure out how to get there. A big part of product leadership is making that outcome clear, choosing what matters, and helping people work through the tradeoffs.</p>
              <p>I like having something we can try and learn from early. That might mean talking through an idea with a customer, building a prototype, or making a small change we can put in front of someone. AI has made it practical for me to do much more of that directly.</p>
              <p>I'm still apprehensive about where all of this is going. But on a personal level, these tools have unlocked me. I can try things I would've struggled to build before, and I keep finding reasons to rethink how I work. That's a lot of what <a href="/writing" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">I write about here</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>

        <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-border">
          <p class="text-text-body leading-relaxed">If something here overlaps with what you're thinking about, <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.author.email}`} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">I'd like to hear from you</a>.</p>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
